    country: "North Korea",
    addedIn: "2026.12",
    module: "TTPs",
    force: "Korean People’s Army",
    echelon: ["Corps"],
    type: "TTP",
    title: "Hardened Artillery Sites: Protected but Fixed",
    what: ["Analysis: North Korea shelters frontline artillery and command posts in Hardened Artillery Sites (HARTS), caves, tunnels and bunkers near the DMZ. They protect guns between salvos, but precision weapons and drones limit their survival in war.", "Refinement: the 2025 Texas National Security Review study says about 170 to 200 HARTS lie within 60 km of Seoul, and about two-thirds of them are simple sites with barracks and above-ground sheds for the guns, not buried tunnels."],
    how: ["Reported: up to 200 HARTS near Seoul shelter 170mm guns and 240mm launchers.", "Reported: tunnels hold guns, FDC bunkers, crew quarters and ammunition niches, separated by blast walls.", "Guns roll out to firing pads or fire from the cave mouth, then pull back inside.", "Reported: survival estimates differ: few guns lasting a week (2012 model), against a 75 percent loss within 10 minutes to an hour from US-ROK guided rockets, radars and missiles (2025 study).", "Reported: in Ukraine, Koksans outside caves were found and struck by HIMARS and drones."],
    why: ["Without the roads, fuel and mobile command to keep thousands of guns moving, North Korea chose concrete and rock; but fixed sites are fixed aim points for guided weapons.", "Compare US and ROK shoot-and-scoot, and the KTSSM built to strike these sites."],
    sources: [{"title": "Lost Seoul: Assessing Pyongyang’s Other Deterrent", "publisher": "Texas National Security Review", "year": "2025", "url": "https://tnsr.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/TNSR-Vol-8-Issue-3_Anderson-Press.pdf"}, {"title": "DPRK Briefing Book: HARTS in North Korea", "publisher": "Nautilus Institute", "year": "", "url": "https://nautilus.org/publications/books/dprkbb/military/dprk-briefing-book-harts-in-north-korea/"}, {"title": "Mind the Gap Between Rhetoric and Reality", "publisher": "Nautilus Institute", "year": "2012", "url": "https://nautilus.org/napsnet/napsnet-special-reports/mind-the-gap-between-rhetoric-and-reality/"}, {"title": "Ukraine Destroys Elusive North Korean Koksan Supergun in Operation Vivaldi", "publisher": "UNITED24 Media", "year": "2026", "url": "https://united24media.com/war-in-ukraine/ukraine-destroys-elusive-north-korean-koksan-supergun-in-operation-vivaldi-23718"}, {"title": "HIMARS Hits Three North Korean M1989 Koksan at Once", "publisher": "Militarnyi", "year": "2025", "url": "https://militarnyi.com/en/news/himars-hits-three-north-korean-m1989-koksan-at-once/"}, {"title": "Lost Seoul? Assessing Pyongyang’s Other Deterrent", "publisher": "Texas National Security Review", "year": "2025", "url": "https://tnsr.org/2025/06/lost-seoul-assessing-pyongyangs-other-deterrent/"}],
    confidence: "Analysis",
    asOf: "2026-11",
